"""run_all_v2.py — collates v2 results into report_v2.md (BUILD-SPEC v2 §5-§7). Implementer: Grace (Claude Fable 5.1), 18 Oct 2026.
Every number below is read from results/ written by calib2.py / analyse.py / pulloff.py / paths.py. targets imported last via compare."""
import sys,os,json,subprocess,numpy as np
HERE=os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); sys.path.insert(0,HERE)
assert 'targets' not in sys.modules
import constants as K
from energy import E_MESH
R=lambda f: json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,'results',f)))
L=[]; A=L.append
gh=subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','--short','HEAD'],cwd=HERE,capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip()
A(f"# Membrane solver v2 — run report (generated by run_all_v2.py)\n\nImplementer: Grace (Claude Fable 5.1), 18 Oct 2026 evening. Spec: `review/2026-10-18/BUILD-SPEC-membrane-solver-v2.md`. Base: the Opus v1 code with v2 §1 fixes F1–F4, F6 and the §3 term; v1 energy kept as `energy_v1.py`. HEAD `{gh}`. Gradients analytic, FD-checked with E1 active (max rel err 5e-8).\n")
A("## 0. Constants (v2 changes)\n\n| name | value |\n|---|---|")
for k in ['K_BEND_FAC','SLING_N','R_GRID','FADE','K_AREA_FAC','K_PEN_FAC','GAP_H','K_NEAR','FADE_EPS']: A(f"| {k} | {getattr(K,k)} |")
A(f"| DELTA_GRID (fm) | {[round(d,4) for d in K.DELTA_GRID]} |\n| Y(2) | {K.Y(2):.6f} MeV |\n| E_MESH | {E_MESH():.6f} MeV |\n")
A("## 1. Added at build time (not in the v2 spec)\n")
A("""| # | what | why | status |
|---|---|---|---|
| B1 | **F7: bending measured from the rest dihedral**, E_bend = K Σ(1 − cos(θ_e − θ_e⁰)) | v2 F1 made inflation stationary at rest but the spec's Helfrich form (1 − cos θ) still charges the icosphere its own curvature: isolated capsid E = 1.5 E₀, max grad 0.57 at rest. With B1 the rest capsid is exactly stationary (E = −4e-17, grad 4e-14). | amber (spec defect 7) |
| B2 | Rows with the deuteron engulfed (closest centroids < 1.3 fm or skin > 1.2 fm from centroid) are marked dead and not pursued | v2 F3 | — |
| B3 | He-4 root search: secant/bisection on E1 with tolerance 0.05 MeV, abandoned when E1 > 6 e₀ | §3 says 'if no root, say so' — a cap defines 'no root' | — |
| B4 | κ = 0.3 E₀ rows added (variant) when all κ = 0.2 rows at r ≥ 3 engulfed | F3 variant | — |
| B5 | Load-path job names include the base state (v1 and v2 paths had collided on file names; the first v2 path reused v1 job files and was discarded: `results/paths_v2_contaminated/`) | bookkeeping bug, found and fixed | — |
| B6 | Fallback F2: T, ³He, ⁴He at the live row with **E1 = e₀ declared** (and E1 = 0 for reference) since no calibrated E1 exists | to produce §5 outputs at all | declared, not a calibration |
""")
st=R('calib2.json')
A("## 2. Calibration (§3) — E₀ from D, then E1 from ⁴He, per (r, δ, κ) row\n")
A("| row | r | δ (fm) | κ/E₀ | E₀ (MeV) | e₀ (MeV/fm²) | D d_min (fm) | ⁴He BE at E1 = 0 | ⁴He BE at the last E1 tried | E1 tried (× e₀) | coop energy there (MeV) | stage / why |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for k,r in st.items():
    row=r['row']; he=r['he4']; done=[e for e in he if e[1] is not None]
    be0=f"{done[0][1]:.3f}" if done else '—'; last=done[-1] if done else None
    A(f"| {k} | {row['r']} | {K.DELTA_GRID[row['di']]:.4f} | {row['kb']} | {r['E0']:.3f} | {r.get('e0',float('nan')):.3f} | {r.get('dmin_D',float('nan')):.2f} | {be0} | {last[1]:.3f} | {last[0]/r['e0']:.2f} | {last[2]['coop']:+.4f} | {r['stage']}: {'; '.join(f for f in r['flags'] if 'variant' not in f)} |" if r['E0'] and last else f"| {k} | {row['r']} | {K.DELTA_GRID[row['di']]:.4f} | {row['kb']} | {r['E0'] if r['E0'] else '—'} | — | {r.get('dmin_D',float('nan')):.2f} | — | — | — | — | {r['stage']}: {'; '.join(r['flags'])} |")
A(f"\nRequired: BE(⁴He) = {K.BE_HE4} MeV. **No row has a root.** In every row where the deuteron is in the contact regime, the cooperative support (skin inside two wells at once) is zero or tiny: patches subtend 19–27° of the capsid and two patches 60° apart do not meet until each exceeds 30°. Where support exists (δ = 0.25 fm, r = 1) E1 = e₀ adds 0.06 MeV to ⁴He against the 23 MeV missing; E1 = 3 e₀ adds 0.23. Reaching ⁴He would need E1 ≈ 400 e₀. The one row that reports a root (r3_d2_kb0.3, E1 = 1.84 e₀) is **spurious**: the ⁴He state at that E1 is a collapsed ball (closest centroids 0.49 fm, skin to 2.08 fm) — the cooperative term is a positive feedback (overlap → coop → more overlap) and the structure jumps first-order from BE 4.0 to 58.7 MeV between E1 = 0.52 and 1.55 MeV/fm². **Rim recovery as skin-sharing has no geometric support at membrane contact sizes, and where it has support it is unstable.** [COMPUTED]\n")
an=R('analyse_fb2.json') if os.path.exists(os.path.join(HERE,'results','analyse_fb2.json')) else {}
meta=R('fb2_meta.json')
A(f"## 3. Fallback F2 — live row {meta['row']} (E₀ = {meta['E0']:.3f} MeV, e₀ = {meta['e0']:.3f} MeV/fm²), E1 = e₀ declared vs E1 = 0\n")
A("| state | BE (MeV) | coop (MeV) | adh (MeV) | mesh | sling | Coulomb | R_ch classical (fm) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for n in ['fb2_T_E1eq_e0','fb2_T_E1_0','fb2_He3_E1eq_e0','fb2_He3_E1_0','fb2_He4_E1eq_e0','fb2_He4_E1_0']:
    if n in an: p=an[n]['parts']; A(f"| {n} | {an[n]['BE']:.3f} | {p['coop']:+.3f} | {p['adh']:+.3f} | {p['mesh']:.3f} | {p['sling']:+.3f} | {p['coul']:.3f} | {an[n]['Rch_classical']:.3f} |")
A("\n### 3.1 Patch geometry (§7.2) at E1 = e₀\n\n| nucleus | pair | d (fm) | E_patch | vertices | aspect | well−geom (hub +) | hub-half |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for n in ['fb2_T_E1eq_e0','fb2_He3_E1eq_e0','fb2_He4_E1eq_e0']:
    if n not in an: continue
    for k,v in an[n]['pairs'].items(): A(f"| {n} | {k} | {v['d']:.3f} | {v['E_patch']:+.3f} | {v['n_vertices']} | {v['aspect']:.3f} | {v.get('well_minus_geom_hub',float('nan')):+.4f} | {v.get('hub_half_fraction',float('nan')):.3f} |")
A("\n**Prediction check (v2 §3, on record):** hub-half fraction in T predicted > 0.55; measured 0.48–0.51. **Prediction fails.** The fat end at the hub does not appear with this term.\n")
A("## 4. Pull-off peel (§4) — F(s) = front width × line energy\n\nAnalytic reference: dome e ∝ (1 − ρ²/a²): axisymmetric peak at ρ*/a = 0.58, stable (tinkle) fraction 0.44; cone: 0.50 / 0.50; v1 rim band w = 0.156a: 0.84 / 0.16.\n")
A("| state | pair | E_patch | axisym F_max (MeV/fm) | ρ*/ρ_max | tinkle (axisym) | tangential F_max | u* (point→hub) | tinkle (tangential) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for n in ['fb2_T_E1eq_e0','fb2_He4_E1eq_e0','fbA_T']:
    f=os.path.join(HERE,'results',f'pulloff_{n}.json')
    if not os.path.exists(f): continue
    for k,v in json.load(open(f)).items():
        ax=v['axisymmetric']; t=v.get('tangential',{}); ur=t.get('u_range',[0,1])
        A(f"| {n} | {k} | {v['E_patch']:.3f} | {ax['F_max']:.3f} | {ax['rho_star']/ax['rho_max']:.2f} | {ax['tinkle_fraction']:.2f} | {t.get('F_max',float('nan')):.3f} | {(t['u_star']-ur[0])/(ur[1]-ur[0]) if t else float('nan'):.2f} | {t.get('tinkle_fraction',float('nan')):.2f} |")
A("\n**Reading:** axisymmetric peaks at 0.54–0.63 of the patch radius with tinkle fractions 0.31–0.47 — the **dome world** (0.58 / 0.44), not the band world (0.84 / 0.16). The well the membrane produces is smooth. [COMPUTED]\n")
A("## 5. Tangential load path on the v2 triton (fb2_T_E1eq_e0; P1 = proton, pivot P3; P2, P3 tethered)\n")
pth=os.path.join(HERE,'results','paths','tangential.json')
if os.path.exists(pth):
    s_=json.load(open(pth)); A(f"Last stable F = **{s_['F_stable']:.4f}** MeV/fm; first unstable F = {s_['hi']}.\n")
    A("| F | snap | roll (°) | P1 spin (°) | P1 shift (fm) | E P1–P2 | E P1–P3 | E P2–P3 | P1–P3 hub-half |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
    for m in sorted(s_['steps'],key=lambda m:m['F']):
        g=lambda k,f: (m['patches'][k] or {}).get(f) or 0
        A(f"| {m['F']:.4f} | {m['snap']}{' (creep)' if m.get('creep') else ''} | {m['theta_roll_deg']:+.2f} | {m['spin_deg']:.2f} | {m['dP1']:.3f} | {g('01','E'):+.3f} | {g('02','E'):+.3f} | {g('12','E'):+.3f} | {g('02','hub_half'):.3f} |")
    po=json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,'results','pulloff_fb2_T_E1eq_e0.json')))['0p-1n']['tangential']['F_max']
    A(f"\n**Cross-check (v2 §4):** the opening component of the applied force on the far patch at snap is 0.5 × F_snap ≈ {0.5*s_['F_stable']:.2f} MeV/fm; the far patch's pull-off peak F_max = {po:.2f} MeV/fm. Ratio {0.5*s_['F_stable']/po:.2f}. On the v1 triton (fbA_T) the same ratio is {0.5*1.85/0.983:.2f}. **The load-path snap is the pull-off peak of the far patch**, to the accuracy of the lever-arm projection. [COMPUTED]\n")
A("## 6. Not run\n\n7.3 quartic mode, 7.6 chain, 7.8 convergence: no calibrated state exists to scale them; radial and out-of-plane paths on the v2 triton (v1 results stand: no peel by 10.2; frictionless below 0.0125).\n")
A("## 7. Comparison with targets (compare.py — last)\n")
import compare
rows={'F2 (E1=e0)':{},'F2 (E1=0)':{}}
for nuc in ['T','He3','He4']:
    for tag,lab in (('E1eq_e0','F2 (E1=e0)'),('E1_0','F2 (E1=0)')):
        n=f'fb2_{nuc}_{tag}'
        if n in an: rows[lab][nuc]=dict(BE=an[n]['BE'],Rch=an[n]['Rch_classical'])
A(compare.table(rows))
A("\nD is calibrated exactly (2.2246) at every row by construction. Classical radii are not quantum rms values.")
open(os.path.join(HERE,'report_v2.md'),'w').write("\n".join(L)+"\n"); print('report_v2.md written',len(L),'lines')
